# CTA Library + Routing Standard

> SEO-local working note (SEO console). The standard CTA blocks for every blog, evergreen URL, and newsletter. Routing follows the balanced/sequenced rule in `05_SEO_TO_REVENUE_MODEL.md`. Applying a CTA to a live URL is a manual beehiiv paste by Al, logged in `04_CHANGE_LOG.md`. Structural standardisation (wiring these into the blog + newsletter templates) is filed for Control. Drafted 2026-06-23. House rules: UK English, no em dashes, §5 clean. Destinations verified live 2026-06-23.

## Verified live destinations
- Advisory: `https://www.masteringobservability.com/advisory` (Book a call + the Observability Assessment, from £5,000)
- Free chapter (lead magnet): `https://www.masteringobservability.com/metrics-and-mayhem/free-chapter`
- The book: `https://www.masteringobservability.com/metrics-and-mayhem/book`
- Newsletter signup: `https://masteringobservability.com`

## Routing rule (which block goes where)
| Intent | Block | Where it goes |
|---|---|---|
| Commercial (cost, strategy, assessment) | **A, Advisory** | Cost Conundrum, Putting It All Together, Harmonising IT, Business-Aligned Observability |
| Informational (definitional, how-to, episodes) | **B, Newsletter** | What Is Grafana Alloy, OpenTelemetry Collector Guide, Signal Drop posts |
| The newsletter itself + book/podcast | **C, Newsletter footer** | every newsletter send, book URL, podcast URL |

---

## Block A, Advisory (commercial URLs)
**Work with me**
If you are leading observability in a regulated enterprise and want an honest read on what is working and what is theatre, I run a fixed-scope Observability Assessment for senior IT and engineering leaders. It ends in a written roadmap and a readout, not a sales deck. (No price in the CTA; the price lives on `/advisory`.)
Book a call or see how it works: https://www.masteringobservability.com/advisory
Not ready to talk? Start with a free chapter of Metrics & Mayhem: https://www.masteringobservability.com/metrics-and-mayhem/free-chapter

## Block B, Newsletter growth (informational URLs)
**Get the next one**
If this was useful, Metrics & Mayhem sends one short, practical piece like it to IT operations leaders most weeks. No fluff, no vendor noise. Join free: https://masteringobservability.com
Or start with a free chapter of the book: https://www.masteringobservability.com/metrics-and-mayhem/free-chapter

## Block C, Newsletter footer (every send) + book/podcast URLs
**Two ways to go deeper**
The book: Metrics & Mayhem: A CTO's Guide to Observability That Actually Works. Kindle is live; paperback and hardback are out. Free chapter: https://www.masteringobservability.com/metrics-and-mayhem/free-chapter
Work with me: a fixed-scope Observability Assessment for senior IT and engineering leaders: https://www.masteringobservability.com/advisory

